<title>MALAYSIA: Kuala Lumpur tin market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Kuala Lumpur tin market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kuala Lumpur tin market is closed from February 6 to February 11 for the twin festivals of Chinese Lunar New Year and Moslem Eid al-Fitr.</p>
<p>Last Wednesday, Malaysia's tin price closed up four cents at 14.31 ringgit ($5.74) a kg, traders said.</p>
<p>Turnover was 112 tonnes, up from 128 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The local price premium over the London Metal Exchange widened to $50 a tonne against $20 previously.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 8911)</p>
